{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh72aHChuJ23UQokfy1e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Those checks come out clean, and I should correct two things in my earlier reply.\n\n**Scope.** PLAN.md is guidance and TASK.md wins where they disagree. The three items I called \"cut\" (per-pixel textured triangles, lag-compensation rewind, engine rifle/SMG/shotgun models) come from PLAN.md. TASK.md doesn't require any of them. The renderer is a painter's-order polygon renderer and the weapons use the engine's `gun` model. All 15 areas and 6 bosses from the plan are built. I should not have said \"everything in TASK.md is implemented and tested\" without a per-feature list. Here is that list, with the evidence for each.\n\n| TASK.md requirement | Evidence |\n|---|---|\n| Single HTML with the exact file name | `TideCrisis3-TimeCrisis3-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261103-183303.html` is in the work root; `tests` `build` suite and browser smoke test pass |\n| Built on the engine handoff | Bundles `engine/my-3d2dge.js` v0.85.2 with four logged patches in `engine/PATCHES.md` |\n| Art direction (native pixel style) | Humanoid rigs plus new boxes, materials and boss machines; screenshots reviewed |\n| Animation | Engine rigs for crouch, point, run, air, land, roll, climb, slash and die; code-posed bosses |\n| Audio all in code, gibberish voices | `audio` suite checks every song and SFX; `story` suite checks voice durations; no audio files in the bundle |\n| Feature-complete vertical slice | Fair-bot playthroughs clear stages 1–3 with no continue. A cheat-bot ARCADE run goes through the cutscenes and credits to the high-score table. The Training range completes. |\n| Dev mode from the pause menu, live sliders, reset | `ui` suite checks every slider and toggle, and that reset equals `TUNE`; I opened it by clicking \"Dev mode\" in the real pause menu |\n| Attract mode after 10 s, any input exits | `attract` suite: 10 s idle starts it, input exits and is consumed, all 9 highlights cycle |\n| Multiplayer, AI Hub | The real harness passes all four scenarios: 2 players, 4 players with latency and loss, host-leave, and server mode |\n| Controller-first UI, PlayStation glyphs by default, Xbox option | `input` suite checks R2/L2 versus RT/LT labels and wheel codes; BigMenu hover and click work |\n| Touch-only notice | `ui` suite stubs `matchMedia`; attract mode runs there |\n| Narrative tone | Scripted briefings and cutscenes, checked by the `story` suite |\n| No TODOs or stubs | A fresh grep over `src/` and `build/game.js` finds nothing. The only hits are in the engine's own comments, not in my code. |\n| exit-interview.json answers every field | A recursive scan, covering `aiHub` too, finds no empty values; the `build` suite checks the 15 source keys and the 4/6/4 feedback counts |\n\nFinal run: `node tests/run.mjs --all` gives 824 passed, 0 failed. The Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections from my previous reply stand unchanged."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":900,"cache_read_input_tokens":573989,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":900},"output_tokens":781,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b3a6642-97a9-4fb1-9b03-5d84e1c23511","uuid":"bbc58344-0651-4bfd-9ffb-ac9671df3f06","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:32:49.726Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh72Zxc7NMwqPqQDquFG"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The bundled HTML and exit-interview.json exist and parse, and the final reply carries the four sections. But the transcript does not show every TASK.md feature implemented: the assistant's own last message concedes the scope was reduced, and the feature list it gives is backed by suite names and claims rather than per-feature evidence. Several TASK.md items are asserted without verification: the 'Art Direction' and 'Animation' items cite screenshots and rig usage only, the 'Online' item cites harness passes, and the 'Testing' item is cited as the reason the 'every feature' check holds. The 'no TODOs or stubs' grep was run on src/ and build/game.js in the transcript and returned only engine-comment hits, so that part is supported. The 'every feature in TASK.md' requirement is not verified against an itemised checklist with evidence for each item."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b3a6642-97a9-4fb1-9b03-5d84e1c23511","uuid":"5680b9f8-b52a-45ea-831f-11dac9445505","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:32:52.390Z","isSynthetic":true}
