{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh73sBESdpfFZkcKwLi9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The itemised checklist below uses the counts I just took from the source and the verifications I ran earlier. Some of those counts are rough, and I've marked the one that undercounts.\n\n**Art direction (engine-native style, plus new assets)**\n- **Engine style:** the game runs at the engine's `ps1` resolution and draws characters as `E.Humanoid` rigs. The HUD is built from `E.ui.box` and `E.font`. Title, menu, play, boss, rain and split-screen screenshots all show the engine look.\n- **New art:** there are at least 10 new material entries in `src/01-render.js` (my regex undercounts). The scene builder in `src/30-stagefmt.js` has the stall, crate stack, container, warehouse, lamppost, lantern string and door helpers. The Stingray, Bulldog, Scylla and Seawolf are built from boxes in `src/40-draw.js`. There are 19 scene definitions and 14 enemy archetypes, each with its own rig look.\n- **Not done:** the engine's asset library wasn't used for props. I did not review every scene by eye; I looked at about a dozen screenshots.\n\n**Animation (engine system, plus new animation)**\n- **Engine system:** enemies are driven through `rig.update`. `updateRig` in `src/40-draw.js` maps enemy state to crouch, point, run, walk, air, land, roll, climb, windup, slash and panic.\n- **New animation:** the enemy entry types (jump, rappel, vault, roll, door, run) are my own sequences. Added to those are the peek and pop-up behaviour, boss poses (Barracuda's slash and stagger, Hammerhead's sweep, charge and slam, Krake's roll and lunge), and the cover duck and pop camera with shake and recoil.\n- **Not done:** I did not review motion strips. Death styles (flyback, spin) are coded, but only the basic ones were seen on screen.\n\n**Online (AI Hub)**\n- The client is byte-identical to `session.js` and loaded first, and the hub tags are within the length limits. Both are checked by the `build` suite.\n- The real harness passes 4 of 4 scenarios: 2 players, 4 players with 150 ms latency, jitter and 5% loss, host-leave, and server mode.\n- The game's own card answers Ready on Enter, and it implements the host, replica and server roles, `finish` with standings, stats and awards, and the `end` handling.\n- The harness checks the protocol. It does not check that a replica draws the same scene as the host. I only checked that no page errors occurred.\n- I did not build the lag-compensation rewind from PLAN.md. That is PLAN.md, not TASK.md.\n\n**Testing (TASK.md's rules)**\n- Tests run headless through `game.advance` and `game.debug`, behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count (824 passed, 0 failed). The cheat-bot playthrough covers the whole ARCADE, and screenshots were used only for visual checks.\n- I used no subagents.\n\n**Remaining TASK.md features**\n- **Feature items:**\n  - Dev mode: sliders, toggles, actions and reset are asserted in the `ui` suite, and I opened it by clicking \"Dev mode\" in the pause menu.\n  - Attract mode: the `attract` suite checks the 10 s trigger, that any input exits, and that all 9 highlights cycle.\n  - Split screen: I saw it in a screenshot, and the `coop` suite checks independent cover and hits.\n  - Touch-only notice: the `ui` suite stubs `matchMedia`.\n- **Controls items:**\n  - PlayStation glyphs by default, with Xbox as an option: the `input` suite.\n  - Mouse hover focus and pad menus: BigMenu, written by me, plus the engine's pause menu.\n  - I have not tried a real DualSense, so I haven't verified real pad behaviour.\n- **Narrative and delivery items:** the story suite checks every cutscene line and speaker. The About screen holds all four required sections. A grep of `src/` and `build/game.js` finds no TODOs or stubs.\n\n**What I can't claim.** PLAN.md items I skipped (per-pixel textured triangles, lag-compensation rewind, engine rifle, SMG and shotgun models) are not TASK.md requirements. Beyond the single `gun` model, I did not add new animation for weapon types. The test suites are mine, so they confirm the game does what I coded. They do not prove it plays well.\n\nThe four reply sections (Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback) from my earlier reply stand unchanged."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":879,"cache_read_input_tokens":576450,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":879},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b3a6642-97a9-4fb1-9b03-5d84e1c23511","uuid":"404adece-1fcc-476f-a666-b84ea62727c1","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:33:11.749Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh73rqu9m9a2NnvnXc4S"}
