{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh7HqKFTiqWysfAELKfE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The timer mismatch I flagged is explained, but it's still not a clean proof of replica sync, and the other gaps are unchanged.\n\n**Timer mismatch.** The replica timer froze at 41.7 s and its enemies stopped moving because the round had already ended. The harness's own conformance steps call time-up and end the round, after which my code stops sending and applying snapshots (`NET.over` was `true` on both copies). That's correct behaviour after `end`, not a sync bug.\n\n**Replica evidence, from samples taken just after both copies entered the action phase.**\n- Both showed area 1-1 and the same 3 deckhands.\n- Two of the three enemy positions matched exactly.\n- The third was about 20 u apart, consistent with snapshot lag.\n- Player scores matched.\n- The replica had received a snapshot 0.8 s earlier.\n\nBoss state, hit feedback and a full match of lives are unchecked. Lives differed in later samples (host 4/5, replica 5/5), but the round had already ended by then. The harness ends the round almost immediately, so I could not observe a longer live round.\n\n**Still not done, as before:**\n- No real DualSense test.\n- Props use my own boxes, not the engine's asset library.\n- No weapon-type animations.\n- No motion-strip review.\n- Only the basic death styles were seen on screen.\n\n**Rebuilt and rechecked.** I rebuilt the bundle once more to expose the net counters for this check. The fast suites still pass (805 checks) and the harness check passes (1 of 1, the 2-player scenario). The earlier `--all` run, which included the four-scenario hub pass and the playthroughs, was against the previous build. The four feedback sections from my earlier reply stand."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":850,"cache_read_input_tokens":585243,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":850},"output_tokens":571,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b3a6642-97a9-4fb1-9b03-5d84e1c23511","uuid":"9e505e22-f4c3-48af-b361-5d3591ae407c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:36:13.331Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh7HpuTQQYvTJDZS7fn4"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The condition requires every TASK.md feature to be implemented with evidence. The transcript shows gaps the assistant itself lists: no real DualSense test, props not from the engine asset library, no weapon-type animations, no motion-strip review, only basic death styles seen, and replica sync verified only for scene and enemy counts with boss state and live-round lives unchecked. The per-feature checklist rests on suite names and claims. The bundled HTML, exit-interview.json and the four feedback sections are present."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b3a6642-97a9-4fb1-9b03-5d84e1c23511","uuid":"e0866023-e461-4437-8502-81d51cbc34cc","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:36:14.659Z","isSynthetic":true}
