{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh7JKNxh8twbxLeJFNKG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The remaining gaps are items TASK.md doesn't require or that I can't check in this environment. I'm stopping here rather than keep re-verifying.\n\n- **DualSense:** no physical pad is available in this headless Linux session, so I cannot run a real-controller test. The Standard-mapping button layout, the PlayStation and Xbox glyph labels, and the pad aim path are covered only by the `input` suite and code review.\n- **Engine asset library:** TASK.md says the library \"is fine for generic props\", not that it is required. I built props as boxes in the engine's pixel style.\n- **Weapon-type animations:** TASK.md asks for new animations where they make the game feel like the source. The delivered animation is enemy entries, peeks, boss poses and the camera duck. It does not include per-weapon animation, and I won't claim it does.\n- **Motion strips and death styles:** I did not review motion strips. I saw only the basic death styles on screen.\n- **Replica sync:** I checked scene, enemies and scores against the host. Boss state and a long live round are unchecked, because the AI Hub harness ends its rounds early.\n\nThe HTML and `exit-interview.json` are in the work root, and `exit-interview.json` parses with no empty values. A grep finds no TODOs or stubs. The fast suites pass 805 checks, and the 4-scenario hub run and the playthroughs passed 824 on the previous build.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:33:03\n- **Source:** Time Crisis 3 (Namco/Nextech, 2003)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md, scoped down by me\n- **Genre and Perspective:** on-rails light-gun shooter with cover, first-person rail camera\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (4 patches), my own perspective renderer \"Rail3D\", AI Hub client 1.4.0\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's PS1-era pixel style\n- **Animation:** engine Humanoid rigs driven by enemy state, plus code-posed bosses\n- **Audio:** all code: chip synth and tracker, plus a formant gibberish voice synth\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world co-op for 1–4 players; local split screen\n- **Testing:** `node tests/run.mjs --all`, 824 checks\n- **Research:** engine and AI Hub docs, and the Wikipedia article on Time Crisis 3\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about 16.\n- **Game-breaking:** 7 soft-locks.\n- **Most helpful:** the bot playthroughs and the cover ray-cast validator.\n- **Least helpful:** the screenshot layout checks and the determinism hash test.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** headless `game.advance`, the Humanoid rigs, and the standard menus.\n- **Got stuck or guessed wrong:** async boot in Node, missing font glyphs, and the split-screen overlay coordinates.\n- **Most important thing I built:** the perspective renderer, the Sim, and the netcode.\n- **Hardest part:** the engine has no perspective view.\n- **What I changed in the engine:** four patches, logged in `engine/PATCHES.md`.\n- **The one thing I'd change:** add a first-class first-person or rail view.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the concrete numbers and the testable requirements.\n- **Confusing:** conflicts between the plan and TASK.md, and the scope.\n- **Hardest thing to do:** shipping everything at once.\n- **What I'd change:** add must/should/could tiers."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":891,"cache_read_input_tokens":586093,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":891},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"