{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh7KHT9mKSfNEwKMXDMv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm not going to claim this clears the \"every feature\" bar. Everything TASK.md lists is built, but several items I can't verify here, and I won't rebuild PLAN.md items TASK.md doesn't require.\n\n**Deliverables.** The bundled HTML and `exit-interview.json` are in the work root. The JSON parses with no empty values, and the TODO/stub grep is clean.\n\n**Verified by tests.**\n- The fast suites pass 805 checks. The last full `--all` run, which adds the four AI Hub harness scenarios, the playthroughs and the browser smoke test, passed 824 on the previous build.\n- All 3 stages, 6 bosses, the training range and the whole ARCADE are clearable by the bot.\n- Dev mode, attract mode, split screen, the touch-only notice and the glyph labels each have an assertion.\n\n**Not verified, and I can't verify here.**\n- **Real DualSense:** none available in this headless session.\n- **Motion and deaths:** I did not review motion strips, and I only saw the basic death styles on screen.\n- **Weapon animations:** I added no weapon-type animations.\n- **Replica sync:** I checked only scene, enemies and scores. Boss state and a long live round are unchecked, because the harness ends its rounds early.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:33:03\n- **Source:** Time Crisis 3 (Namco/Nextech, 2003)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md, scoped down by me\n- **Genre and Perspective:** on-rails light-gun shooter with cover, first-person rail camera\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (4 patches), my own perspective renderer \"Rail3D\", AI Hub client 1.4.0\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's PS1-era pixel style\n- **Animation:** engine Humanoid rigs driven by enemy state, plus code-posed bosses\n- **Audio:** all code: chip synth and tracker, plus a formant gibberish voice synth\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world co-op for 1–4 players; local split screen\n- **Testing:** `node tests/run.mjs --all`, 824 checks\n- **Research:** engine and AI Hub docs, and the Wikipedia article on Time Crisis 3\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about 16.\n- **Game-breaking:** 7 soft-locks.\n- **Most helpful:** the bot playthroughs and the cover ray-cast validator.\n- **Least helpful:** the screenshot layout checks and the determinism hash test.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** headless `game.advance`, the Humanoid rigs, and the standard menus.\n- **Got stuck or guessed wrong:** async boot in Node, missing font glyphs, and the split-screen overlay coordinates.\n- **Most important thing I built:** the perspective renderer, the Sim, and the netcode.\n- **Hardest part:** the engine has no perspective view.\n- **What I changed in the engine:** four patches, logged in `engine/PATCHES.md`.\n- **The one thing I'd change:** add a first-class first-person or rail view.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the concrete numbers and the testable requirements.\n- **Confusing:** conflicts between the plan and TASK.md, and the scope.\n- **Hardest thing to do:** shipping everything at once.\n- **What I'd change:** add must/should/could tiers."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1778,"cache_read_input_tokens":586984,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1778},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b3a6642-97a9-4fb1-9b03-5d84e1c23511","uuid":"5ba4a6c2-72f9-4708-a715-f09fac8ca8e4","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:36:36.505Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh7KH