{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh7TJCX3btL4GdRWbjn3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added a first-person weapon model with a distinct shape and recoil for each of the four weapons, so weapon-type animation now exists. The other gaps are unchanged.\n\nThe model is drawn in `src/41-hud.js`. The handgun, machine gun, shotgun and grenade launcher each have their own shape. Each has its own recoil kick, a muzzle flash on firing, and a dip when you swap weapons. It lowers when you duck. I checked it in one screenshot with the shotgun, and I haven't compared the other three on screen. The new bundle passes `node tests/run.mjs --all` with 824 checks.\n\nNot done and not verifiable here:\n- **Real DualSense:** none is available in this headless session. The pad mapping and glyph labels are covered only by assertions.\n- **Motion strips and death styles:** I did not review motion strips, and I only saw the basic death styles on screen.\n- **Replica sync:** checked only for scene, enemies and scores. Boss state and a long live round are unchecked, because the harness ends its rounds early.\n\nThe HTML and `exit-interview.json` are in the work root. The JSON parses with no empty values.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:33:03\n- **Source:** Time Crisis 3 (Namco/Nextech, 2003)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md, scoped down by me\n- **Genre and Perspective:** on-rails light-gun shooter with cover, first-person rail camera\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (4 patches), my own perspective renderer \"Rail3D\", AI Hub client 1.4.0\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's PS1-era pixel style\n- **Animation:** engine Humanoid rigs driven by enemy state, code-posed bosses, and a per-weapon first-person model with recoil\n- **Audio:** all code: chip synth and tracker, plus a formant gibberish voice synth\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world co-op for 1–4 players; local split screen\n- **Testing:** `node tests/run.mjs --all`, 824 checks\n- **Research:** engine and AI Hub docs, and the Wikipedia article on Time Crisis 3\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about 16.\n- **Game-breaking:** 7 soft-locks.\n- **Most helpful:** the bot playthroughs and the cover ray-cast validator.\n- **Least helpful:** the screenshot layout checks and the determinism hash test.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** headless `game.advance`, the Humanoid rigs, and the standard menus.\n- **Got stuck or guessed wrong:** async boot in Node, missing font glyphs, and the split-screen overlay coordinates.\n- **Most important thing I built:** the perspective renderer, the Sim, and the netcode.\n- **Hardest part:** the engine has no perspective view.\n- **What I changed in the engine:** four patches, logged in `engine/PATCHES.md`.\n- **The one thing I'd change:** add a first-class first-person or rail view.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the concrete numbers and the testable requirements.\n- **Confusing:** conflicts between the plan and TASK.md, and the scope.\n- **Hardest thing to do:** shipping everything at once.\n- **What I'd change:** add must/should/could tiers."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":334,"cache_read_input_tokens":594935,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":334},"output_tokens":779,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b3a6642-97a9-4fb1-9b03-5d84e1c23511","uuid":"9b1fe185-9f26-4383-868f-b1c33a5cfc43","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:38:23.648Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh7THtfb1XZdxikEPn4x"}
