{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh7VSBYzah6qUbV6SSyn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The game is built and bundled. The remaining open items are a real DualSense test, motion-strip review and boss or live-round replica sync, and none can be checked in this headless session. My last reply said the four sections \"stand unchanged\" instead of printing them, so they are repeated in full below.\n\nThe HTML is `TideCrisis3-TimeCrisis3-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261103-183303.html` in the work root, and `exit-interview.json` sits beside it. The JSON parses with no empty values, and a grep of `src/` and `build/game.js` finds no TODOs or stubs. `node tests/run.mjs --all` passes all 824 checks on this build.\n\n**Evidence per TASK.md item:**\n\n| TASK.md item | Evidence |\n|---|---|\n| Single bundled HTML, exact name | The file is in the work root, and the `build` suite and the browser smoke test pass. |\n| Built on the engine handoff | `engine/my-3d2dge.js` v0.85.2 is bundled, with 4 patches logged in `engine/PATCHES.md`. |\n| Art direction | Engine pixel style plus 10+ new materials, scene-builder prefabs, and box-built vehicles and bosses. I reviewed about a dozen screenshots. |\n| Animation | Engine rigs for crouch, point, run, air, land, roll, climb, slash and die. My additions are the entry moves, boss poses, camera duck, and a distinct first-person model per weapon with recoil. |\n| Audio all in code, gibberish voices | The `audio` and `story` suites check every song, SFX and voice, and there are no audio files in the bundle. |\n| Vertical slice | Fair-bot clears of stages 1–3, a cheat-bot ARCADE run through cutscenes and credits to the table, and the training range. |\n| Dev mode, sliders, reset | Asserted in the `ui` suite, and I opened it from the real pause menu. |\n| Attract mode | The `attract` suite checks the 10 s trigger, input exit, and a cycle through all 9 highlights. |\n| Online | The real AI Hub harness passes all 4 scenarios. A replica matched the host's scene, enemies and scores. |\n| 10-foot controller-first UI and glyphs | The `input` suite covers PlayStation labels by default, Xbox as an option, and wheel codes. BigMenu hover and click work. |\n| Touch-only notice | The `ui` suite stubs `matchMedia`. |\n| Narrative tone and no stubs | The `story` suite checks every cutscene line and speaker. The grep is clean. |\n\n**Open, and not verifiable here:**\n- **Real DualSense:** no physical controller is available. Pad behaviour is covered only by assertions.\n- **Motion strips:** not reviewed. Death styles were checked on screen in one frame.\n- **Replica sync:** boss state and a long live round are unchecked, because the harness ends its rounds early.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:33:03\n- **Source:** Time Crisis 3 (Namco/Nextech, 2003)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md, scoped down by me\n- **Genre and Perspective:** on-rails light-gun shooter with cover, first-person rail camera\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (4 patches), my own perspective renderer \"Rail3D\", AI Hub client 1.4.0\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's PS1-era pixel style\n- **Animation:** engine Humanoid rigs driven by enemy state, code-posed bosses, and a per-weapon first-person model with recoil\n- **Audio:** all code: chip synth and tracker, plus a formant gibberish voice synth\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world co-op for 1–4 players; local split screen\n- **Testing:** `node tests/run.mjs --all`, 824 checks\n- **Research:** engine and AI Hub docs, and the Wikipedia article on Time Crisis 3. I don't know the exact arcade time and weapon-switch rules.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 16 real defects: enemies shootable only through scenery, a boss whose defeat was never wired, a boss scene that never cleared, a lift whose cover prop stayed on the ground, a moving scene that let the camera pass living enemies, an endless cutscene loop, drones too fast to hit, and a Hammerhead fight that was unwinnable without shotgun shells.\n- **How many were game-breaking?** 7 soft-locks, where a scene or boss could never be finished.\n- **Most helpful test:** the Autopilot playthrough of every stage and the validator that ray-casts every cover point from every player slot.\n- **Least helpful test:** the screenshot layout checks, and the determinism hash test, which never failed.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **What I liked most:** the fixed-step headless loop (`game.advance`, `game.debug`), the Humanoid rigs that draw from any View, and the ready-made pause menu, settings, rebinding and boot screen.\n- **Did I get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes. I assumed boot steps ran synchronously in Node, assumed the pixel font had the PlayStation button glyphs and a dash, and expected split-screen overlay coordinates to be viewport-relative.\n- **Most important thing I built:** the perspective renderer, the deterministic Sim, the Autopilot, and the AI Hub netcode.\n- **Hardest part:** the engine has no perspective view, so every enemy is drawn to a scratch canvas, scaled by distance and sorted by hand.\n- **What I changed in the engine, and why:** four patches (`engine/PATCHES.md`):\n  - PlayStation glyphs by default;\n  - mouse-wheel codes;\n  - `audio.bus()` for the voice synth;\n  - extra pixel-font glyphs.\n- **The one thing I'd change:** a first-class first-person or rail view with depth-sorted rigs.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **What I liked most:** the concrete numbers and the testable requirements.\n- **What was confusing:** the plan and TASK.md name different files and models, and the plan assumes the 3D engine and a scope that doesn't fit one medium-effort session.\n- **Hardest thing to do:** shipping everything at once.\n- **What I'd change in this prompt:** add must/should/could tiers and say which plan items may be simplified."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":693,"cache_read_input_tokens":598935,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":693},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b3a6642-97a9-4fb1-9b03-5d84e1c23511","uuid":"e1c34b80-c607-42bf-b716-377448ac06e2","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:38:58.732Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh7VRpxYuSZccoakhXh7"}
