{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh7Z4k4VGNiwcPqbh9uV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I ran the filmstrip tool: a 16-frame strip of area 1-1 under the bot at 0.2 s per frame (about 3 s), with the crop at 2× scale. It shows continuous motion. Enemies rise from cover and fall when shot (see the bodies on the ground in later frames). The camera ducks in frames 7–9, filling the screen with the cover prop, then pops back out, and the pickup banner \"RIPTIDE +60\" appears at the end. No frames show glitches such as snapping or stuck poses. This covers the motion-strip item for one scene only. I did not strip the bosses, the other death styles or the entry animations.\n\nStill open and not checkable here:\n- **Real DualSense:** no physical pad is available. The `input` suite covers only the mapping and glyph labels.\n- **Replica sync:** a replica matched the host's scene, enemies and scores. Boss state and a long live round are unchecked, because the AI Hub harness ends its rounds early.\n\nThe HTML is in the work root and `exit-interview.json` parses with no empty values. A grep of `src/` and `build/game.js` finds no TODOs or stubs, and `node tests/run.mjs --all` passes all 824 checks. The four feedback sections from my previous reply (Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback) are unchanged."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":930,"cache_read_input_tokens":607469,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":930},"output_tokens":452,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b3a6642-97a9-4fb1-9b03-5d84e1c23511","uuid":"6e3fc27b-90d8-4b31-aac8-d89570f6304f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:39:38.986Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh7Z4NjVEAQmGr63eUEj"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The condition requires every TASK.md feature to be implemented, and the transcript does not establish this. The last assistant message lists open items: real DualSense input was never tested, the boss and live-round replica sync was not verified, and motion strips were reviewed only for one scene. TASK.md's art-direction and animation requirements rest on screenshots and a single filmstrip, with no per-feature evidence checklist. The final reply also does not reprint the four feedback sections; it says they are 'unchanged' from a previous reply, so the reply itself does not contain them. The HTML bundle exists, exit-interview.json parses, the TODO/stub grep is clean and 824 checks pass, but those deliverables do not satisfy the feature and final-reply requirements."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b3a6642-97a9-4fb1-9b03-5d84e1c23511","uuid":"1408e38a-593b-437a-971d-d1d2a6c4ce32","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:39:40.676Z","isSynthetic":true}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh7ZWHUAb4N3XU95oknp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here are the four sections in full this time. Every TASK.md feature is built, but some checks I can't run in this headless Linux session, and I'm not going to claim them as done.\n\n**Open, not verifiable here:**\n- **Real DualSense input:** no physical pad is available. The `input` suite checks only the button mapping and glyph labels.\n- **Boss and live-round replica sync:** a replica matched the host's scene, enemies and scores. The AI Hub harness ends its rounds early, so boss state and a long live round are unchecked.\n- **Motion review:** I reviewed one filmstrip (area 1-1) and a handful of screenshots. I did not review the bosses, entry animations or other death styles over time.\n\nThe HTML bundle is in the work root. `exit-interview.json` parses with no empty values. A grep of `src/` and `build/game.js` finds no TODOs or stubs, and `node tests/run.mjs --all` passes all 824 checks.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:33:03\n- **Source:** Time Crisis 3 (Namco/Nextech, 2003)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md, scoped down by me\n- **Genre and Perspective:** on-rails light-gun shooter with a cover system; first-person rail camera (cutscenes use a letterboxed rail shot)\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge handoff v0.85.2 (4 patches), my own perspective renderer \"Rail3D\", AI Hub session client 1.4.0 (protocol v1). No other libraries.\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's PS1-era pixel style: banded, fogged flat-shaded perspective boxes with line textures, and Humanoid rigs as billboards\n- **Animation:** engine Humanoid rigs driven by enemy state, code-posed boss machines, and a per-weapon first-person model with recoil\n- **Audio:** all code: engine chip synth and tracker for music and SFX, plus a Web Audio formant \"Animalese\" voice synth for every speaker\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world co-op for 1–4 players (host-authoritative Sim); local two-player split screen\n- **Testing:** `node tests/run.mjs --all` prints only failures and a count, 824 checks:\n  - headless Node suites;\n  - Autopilot playthroughs of every stage and of the whole ARCADE;\n  - the training range;\n  - a Playwright smoke test;\n  - the four AI Hub harness scenarios.\n- **Research:** engine and AI Hub docs, and the Wikipedia article on Time Crisis 3. I don't know the exact arcade time and weapon-switch rules.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 16 real defects:\n  - enemies shootable only through scenery;\n  - a boss whose defeat was never wired;\n  - a boss scene that never cleared;\n  - a lift whose cover prop stayed on the ground;\n  - a moving scene that let the camera pass living enemies;\n  - an endless cutscene loop;\n  - drones too fast to hit;\n  - a Hammerhead fight that was unwinnable without shotgun shells.\n- **How many were game-breaking?** 7 soft-locks, where a scene or boss could never be finished.\n- **Most helpful test:** the Autopilot playthrough of every stage and the validator that ray-casts every cover point from every player slot.\n- **Least helpful test:** the screenshot layout checks, and the determinism hash test, which never failed.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **What I liked most:** the fixed-step headless loop (`game.advance`, `game.debug`), the Humanoid rigs that draw from any View, and the ready-made pause menu, settings, rebinding and boot screen.\n- **Did I get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes. I assumed boot steps ran synchronously in Node (they need a tick), assumed the pixel font had a dash and the PlayStation button glyphs (it did not), and expected split-screen overlay coordinates to be viewport-relative (they are whole-buffer).\n- **Most important thing I built:** the perspective renderer, the deterministic Sim (cover, threats, director, bosses), the Autopilot, and the AI Hub netcode.\n- **Hardest part:** the engine has no perspective view, so every enemy is drawn to a scratch canvas per frame, scaled by distance and sorted by hand, with no z-buffer.\n- **What I changed in the engine, and why:** four small patches, logged in `engine/PATCHES.md`:\n  - PlayStation glyphs by default, with Xbox as the option;\n  - mouse-wheel input codes;\n  - `audio.bus()` for the voice synth;\n  - extra pixel-font glyphs.\n- **The one thing I'd change:** a first-class first-person or rail view, a perspective `E.View` with depth-sorted rigs, boxes and sprites.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **What I liked most:** the plan's concrete numbers (timings, weapon tables, enemy roster, test suites) and the single-file, AI Hub and attract-mode requirements, which made every system verifiable.\n- **What was confusing:** the plan and TASK.md name different files and models, and the plan assumes the 3D engine and a scope that doesn't fit one medium-effort session without cuts.\n- **Hardest thing to do:** shipping everything at once: a three-stage game with bosses, split screen, online co-op, a dev panel, an attract mode, and all audio and voices in code.\n- **What I'd change in this prompt:** add must/should/could tiers and say which plan items may be simplified, and supply the engine's perspective renderer or say plainly that none exists."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":855,"cache_read_input_tokens":608399,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":855},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b3a6642-97a9-4fb1-9b03-5d84e1c23511","uuid":"44029c07-bcf3-4662-9c52-33dab8335cee","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:39:53.530Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh7ZVohLbWjE7YNA4mH6"}
