{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh7aYyDed8mWHUTAZb72","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Every feature TASK.md lists is built and tested. The three checks I can't run here, DualSense input, boss and live-round replica sync, and a motion review beyond area 1-1, are still unverified. I won't claim them as done.\n\n- **Real DualSense:** the `input` suite covers only the button mapping and glyph labels, because no physical pad is available.\n- **Boss and live-round replica sync:** a replica matched the host's scene, enemies and scores. The AI Hub harness ends its rounds early, so I couldn't observe boss state or a long live round.\n- **Motion review:** one filmstrip of area 1-1 shows continuous motion with no glitches. Bosses, entry animations and most death styles were not reviewed over time.\n\nThe HTML bundle is in the work root. `exit-interview.json` parses with no empty values. The grep for TODOs and stubs is clean, and `node tests/run.mjs --all` passes all 824 checks.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:33:03\n- **Source:** Time Crisis 3 (Namco/Nextech, 2003)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md, scoped down by me\n- **Genre and Perspective:** on-rails light-gun shooter with cover; first-person rail camera\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (4 patches), my own perspective renderer \"Rail3D\", AI Hub client 1.4.0\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's PS1-era pixel style\n- **Animation:** engine Humanoid rigs, code-posed bosses, and a per-weapon first-person model with recoil\n- **Audio:** all code: chip synth and tracker, plus a formant gibberish voice synth\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world co-op for 1–4 players; local split screen\n- **Testing:** `node tests/run.mjs --all`, 824 checks\n- **Research:** engine and AI Hub docs, and the Wikipedia article on Time Crisis 3\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about 16 real defects, including enemies shootable only through scenery, a boss whose defeat was never wired, a lift with no cover, and an endless cutscene loop.\n- **Game-breaking:** 7 soft-locks.\n- **Most helpful:** the Autopilot playthroughs and the cover ray-cast validator.\n- **Least helpful:** the screenshot layout checks and the determinism hash test.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** headless `game.advance`, the Humanoid rigs, and the standard menus.\n- **Got stuck or guessed wrong:** async boot in Node, missing font glyphs, and split-screen overlay coordinates.\n- **Most important thing I built:** the perspective renderer, the Sim, and the netcode.\n- **Hardest part:** the engine has no perspective view.\n- **What I changed in the engine:** four patches, logged in `engine/PATCHES.md`.\n- **The one thing I'd change:** add a first-class first-person or rail view.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the concrete numbers and the testable requirements.\n- **Confusing:** conflicts between the plan and TASK.md, and the scope.\n- **Hardest thing to do:** shipping everything at once.\n- **What I'd change:** add must/should/could tiers."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2373,"cache_read_input_tokens":609254,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2373},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b3a6642-97a9-4fb1-9b03-5d84e1c23511","uuid":"a6c82ee6-30f0-4bb0-b1d3-f357de65fbb3","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:40:02.380Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh7aYe8Bwvb24kvfEF2D"}
