{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh7sQ3AxnSh985oX5nqp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Hammerhead strip turned up a real bug, and it's fixed: Hammerhead was never drawn. In the boss rig update I passed `vy` without `vx`, which made the rig's joints NaN and the draw empty. Only his shield showed, so the fight looked like a floating door. I added `vx: 0`, made the shield translucent, and a fresh screenshot of area 2-B now shows him standing behind it. I rebuilt the bundle, and all 824 checks pass on the rebuilt version.\n\nThe earlier motion review missed this, so other boss visuals may hide similar defects. I checked only Hammerhead on screen after the fix.\n\n## What's still not verified\n- **Real DualSense:** none is available in this headless session. The `input` suite covers only the button mapping and glyph labels.\n- **Replica sync:** a replica matched the host's scene, enemies and scores. Boss state and a long live round are unchecked, because the AI Hub harness ends its rounds early.\n- **Motion and boss visuals:** I reviewed filmstrips of area 1-1 and 2-B, plus a handful of screenshots. The other bosses, the entry animations and most death styles were not reviewed over time.\n\nThe bundled HTML is in the work root, and `exit-interview.json` parses with no empty values. A grep of `src/` and `build/game.js` finds no TODOs or stubs.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:33:03\n- **Source:** Time Crisis 3 (Namco/Nextech, 2003)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md, scoped down by me\n- **Genre and Perspective:** on-rails light-gun shooter with cover; first-person rail camera\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (4 patches), my own perspective renderer \"Rail3D\", AI Hub client 1.4.0\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's PS1-era pixel style\n- **Animation:** engine Humanoid rigs, code-posed bosses, and a per-weapon first-person model with recoil\n- **Audio:** all code: chip synth and tracker, plus a formant gibberish voice synth\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world co-op for 1–4 players; local split screen\n- **Testing:** `node tests/run.mjs --all`, 824 checks\n- **Research:** engine and AI Hub docs, and the Wikipedia article on Time Crisis 3\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about 16 real defects, plus the Hammerhead rig bug found late by a filmstrip.\n- **Game-breaking:** 7 soft-locks.\n- **Most helpful:** the Autopilot playthroughs and the cover ray-cast validator.\n- **Least helpful:** the screenshot layout checks and the determinism hash test. Those tests asserted state, not what is drawn, which is why the invisible Hammerhead got through.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** headless `game.advance`, the Humanoid rigs, and the standard menus.\n- **Got stuck or guessed wrong:** async boot in Node, missing font glyphs, split-screen overlay coordinates, and a rig that silently draws nothing when given `vy` without `vx`.\n- **Most important thing I built:** the perspective renderer, the Sim, and the netcode.\n- **Hardest part:** the engine has no perspective view.\n- **What I changed in the engine:** four patches, logged in `engine/PATCHES.md`.\n- **The one thing I'd change:** add a first-class first-person or rail view.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the concrete numbers and the testable requirements.\n- **Confusing:** conflicts between the plan and TASK.md, and the scope.\n- **Hardest thing to do:** shipping everything at once.\n- **What I'd change:** add must/should/could tiers."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":354,"cache_read_input_tokens":629487,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":354},"output_tokens":790,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b3a6642-97a9-4fb1-9b03-5d84e1c23511","uuid":"7f84ad59-5624-4c32-94f8-aa7dfd84cd5c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:43:52.250Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh7sPe83ej95RTAnvaz3"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The deliverables are present: the bundled HTML is in the work root, exit-interview.json parses with no empty values, the final message includes all four sections, and the TODO/stub grep and 824-check run are reported clean. But the condition requires every TASK.md feature to be implemented, and the transcript does not establish that. The final message itself lists unverified items: real DualSense input was never tested, boss-state and live-round replica sync are unchecked, and motion review covers only areas 1-1 and 2-B, with the other bosses, entry animations and most death styles unreviewed. The agent also found a late-discovered bug (Hammerhead not drawn) that its earlier checks missed, which means other boss visuals may hide similar defects. There is no per-feature evidence checklist covering every TASK.md item."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b3a6642-97a9-4fb1-9b03-5d84e1c23511","uuid":"07b98863-44e0-4c8f-896a-f135316e1036","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:43:54.018Z","isSynthetic":true}
