{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh7z58aPbUV9kppThAJM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed a 16-frame filmstrip of the enemy entry moves in area 1-1, shown at 2× scale, with jump, vault, roll, rappel and run-in all spawned at once. It shows continuous motion with no frozen or snapping poses. An enemy drops in from above, another arcs over cover (the dark figures mid-air in the early frames), and a runner crosses open floor into view in the last frames. Crisis rings and tracers fire during the sequence, and a few enemies peek and duck at their covers.\n\nThe strip is too small to judge fine detail such as the rappel rope, the roll rotation or landing frames. I looked at it once, and I'm not claiming a frame-by-frame review.\n\n- **Real DualSense:** no physical pad is available in this headless session. The `input` suite covers only the button mapping and glyph labels.\n- **Replica sync:** a replica matched the host's scene, enemies and scores. The AI Hub harness ends its rounds early, so boss state and a long live round are unchecked.\n- **Motion review:** this is now four filmstrips (areas 1-1 and 2-B, plus this one) and screenshots of every boss. Most death styles were seen only as final poses on screen.\n\nThe bundled HTML is in the work root, and `exit-interview.json` parses with no empty values. A grep of `src/` and `build/game.js` finds no TODOs or stubs, and `node tests/run.mjs --all` passes all 824 checks.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:33:03\n- **Source:** Time Crisis 3 (Namco/Nextech, 2003)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md, scoped down by me\n- **Genre and Perspective:** on-rails light-gun shooter with a cover system; first-person rail camera\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (4 patches), my own perspective renderer \"Rail3D\", AI Hub client 1.4.0\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's PS1-era pixel style\n- **Animation:** engine Humanoid rigs, code-posed boss machines, and a per-weapon first-person model with recoil\n- **Audio:** all code: chip synth and tracker, plus a formant gibberish voice synth\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world co-op for 1–4 players; local split screen\n- **Testing:** `node tests/run.mjs --all`, 824 checks\n- **Research:** engine and AI Hub docs, and the Wikipedia article on Time Crisis 3. I don't know the exact arcade time and weapon-switch rules.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about 16 real defects, plus a late visual bug (Hammerhead never drawn) found by a filmstrip.\n- **Game-breaking:** 7 soft-locks.\n- **Most helpful:** the Autopilot playthroughs and the cover ray-cast validator.\n- **Least helpful:** the screenshot layout checks and the determinism hash test. My assertions covered state, not what was drawn.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** headless `game.advance`, the Humanoid rigs, and the standard menus.\n- **Got stuck or guessed wrong:** async boot in Node, missing font glyphs, split-screen overlay coordinates, and a rig that silently draws nothing when given `vy` without `vx`.\n- **Most important thing I built:** the perspective renderer, the Sim, and the netcode.\n- **Hardest part:** the engine has no perspective view.\n- **What I changed in the engine:** four patches, logged in `engine/PATCHES.md`.\n- **The one thing I'd change:** add a first-class first-person or rail view.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the concrete numbers and the testable requirements.\n- **Confusing:** conflicts between the plan and TASK.md, and the scope.\n- **Hardest thing to do:** shipping everything at once.\n- **What I'd change:** add must/should/could tiers."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1707,"cache_read_input_tokens":640647,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1707},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b3a6642-97a9-4fb1-9b03-5d84e1c23511","uuid":"e753e4cb-0690-42b6-b33e-16b1993e2b21","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:45:23.853Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh7z4hGyGSETPHKi7AWw"}
