{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh7zz8yWrdDMXNfERvp4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything TASK.md asks for is built, but three things stay unverified, and no further work in this session can change that.\n\n- **Real DualSense input:** there is no physical pad in this headless Linux session. The `input` suite checks the button mapping and the PlayStation and Xbox glyph labels, not a real controller.\n- **Replica sync:** a replica matched the host's scene, enemies and scores. The AI Hub harness ends its rounds early, so boss state and a long live round are unchecked.\n- **Motion:** I reviewed four filmstrips (areas 1-1 and 2-B, and the entry moves) and screenshots of every boss. Most death styles were seen only as final poses.\n\nHere is each TASK.md item against its evidence:\n\n| TASK.md item | Evidence |\n|---|---|\n| Single HTML with the exact name | The file is in the work root. The `build` suite and the browser smoke test pass. |\n| Built on the engine handoff | Engine v0.85.2, with 4 patches logged in `engine/PATCHES.md`. |\n| Art direction and animation | Engine-style rigs and my own materials and boss models, reviewed in about 20 screenshots and 4 filmstrips. |\n| Audio all in code, gibberish voices | The `audio` and `story` suites. The bundle has no audio files. |\n| Feature-complete vertical slice | The bot clears all 3 stages. A cheat-bot ARCADE run reaches the credits and the high-score table. The training range completes. |\n| Dev mode, attract mode, touch-only notice, split screen | Asserted in the `ui`, `attract` and `coop` suites. I also opened dev mode from the real pause menu. |\n| AI Hub online | The real harness passes all 4 scenarios. |\n| 10-foot, controller-first UI and glyphs | The `input` suite plus screenshots. |\n| No TODOs or stubs, exit interview | The grep is clean. `exit-interview.json` parses with no empty values. |\n\n`node tests/run.mjs --all` passes all 824 checks on the current build.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:33:03\n- **Source:** Time Crisis 3 (Namco/Nextech, 2003)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md, scoped down by me\n- **Genre and Perspective:** on-rails light-gun shooter with a cover system; first-person rail camera\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (4 patches), my own perspective renderer \"Rail3D\", AI Hub client 1.4.0\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's PS1-era pixel style\n- **Animation:** engine Humanoid rigs, code-posed boss machines, and a per-weapon first-person model with recoil\n- **Audio:** all code: chip synth and tracker, plus a formant gibberish voice synth\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world co-op for 1–4 players; local split screen\n- **Testing:** `node tests/run.mjs --all`, 824 checks\n- **Research:** engine and AI Hub docs, and the Wikipedia article on Time Crisis 3. I don't know the exact arcade time and weapon-switch rules.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 16 real defects, plus a late visual bug: Hammerhead was never drawn.\n- **How many were game-breaking?** 7 soft-locks.\n- **Most helpful test:** the Autopilot playthroughs and the cover ray-cast validator.\n- **Least helpful test:** the screenshot layout checks and the determinism hash test.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **What I liked most:** headless `game.advance`, the Humanoid rigs, and the standard menus.\n- **Did I get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes: async boot in Node, missing font glyphs, split-screen overlay coordinates, and a rig that draws nothing when given `vy` without `vx`.\n- **Most important thing I built:** the perspective renderer, the Sim, and the netcode.\n- **Hardest part:** the engine has no perspective view.\n- **What I changed in the engine, and why:** four patches, logged in `engine/PATCHES.md`.\n- **The one thing I'd change:** add a first-class first-person or rail view.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **What I liked most:** the concrete numbers and the testable requirements.\n- **What was confusing:** conflicts between the plan and TASK.md, and the scope.\n- **Hardest thing to do:** shipping everything at once.\n- **What I'd change:** add must/should/could tiers."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1909,"cache_read_input_tokens":642354,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1909},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b3a6642-97a9-4fb1-9b03-5d84e1c23511","uuid":"44adc6cc-4c7c-4435-938d-bacb834008a9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:45:36.605Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh7zyndgA5M4FY698GeK"}
